1
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:13,140
The exercise library holds every drill your staff uses — text, video, photo or diagram — shared with your colleagues.

2
00:00:13,140 --> 00:00:17,509
Search or filter to find a drill in seconds.

3
00:00:17,509 --> 00:00:24,985
Open it. Each exercise learns from real sessions: what was planned, and the effort players actually reported.

4
00:00:24,985 --> 00:00:34,309
Plan a session lists the week’s trainings, each tagged against the next match.

5
00:00:34,309 --> 00:00:40,230
Open Tuesday’s training: 90 minutes planned, ready for the 18 players called up.

6
00:00:40,230 --> 00:00:45,374
Edit the running order to build the session block by block.

7
00:00:45,374 --> 00:00:54,384
Every block has its start time, duration, planned RPE and load in AU — and links to drills from your library.

8
00:00:54,384 --> 00:01:01,857
Your library sits on the left: search it, preview a drill, then drag it into the session.

9
00:01:01,857 --> 00:01:07,774
Totals update as you go: duration, load, average RPE and number of blocks.

10
00:01:07,774 --> 00:01:15,226
Click Done. The plan feeds the week’s planned load, and the live session view on the pitch.
